{"title":"2023 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 18","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_3.1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3.1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(Easy_to_understand_and_simple)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (Easy to understand and simple)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Math-X_(Smart_and_Simple)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Math-X (Smart and Simple)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_STEM_Station(Quick_and_Easy_to_Understand)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by STEM Station(Quick and Easy to Understand)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Pi_Academy_(Fast_and_Easy)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Pi Academy (Fast and Easy)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(A_Clever_Explanation_You’ll_Get_Instantly)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (A Clever Explanation You’ll Get Instantly)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#Animated_Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">12</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Animated Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-13\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn_(Restrictive_Counting)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">13</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn (Restrictive Counting)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-14\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Magic_Square\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">14</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Magic Square</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-15\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Interstigation\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">15</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Interstigation</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-16\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_harungurcan\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">16</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by harungurcan</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-17\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Dr._David\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">17</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Dr. David</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-18\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_WhyMath\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">18</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by WhyMath</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-19\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_SquishBJ_(AIME_Qualifier)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">19</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by SquishBJ (AIME Qualifier)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-20\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">20</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Greta Grasshopper sits on a long line of lily pads in a pond. From any lily pad, Greta can jump <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> pads to the right or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> pads to the left. What is the fewest number of jumps Greta must make to reach the lily pad located <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/7/0873e9fed23538e535ac05c3284b86bd7bce6fd6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2023$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> pads to the right of her starting position?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/2/d62dea04d0d8fd55358df075b37507238daa5de1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) } 405 \\qquad \\textbf{(B) } 407 \\qquad \\textbf{(C) } 409 \\qquad \\textbf{(D) } 411 \\qquad \\textbf{(E) } 413$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"446\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> directions going <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> right or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> left. We can assign a variable to each of these directions. We can call going right <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> direction <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/e/4ae5f1c3bb5ee22198c136ad4cc3dda97286f0d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{X}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"12\" height=\"12\" /> and we can call going <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> left <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/f/fcfb65d98e3e4d7d8592056f225e7e1bddebf4d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{Y}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"12\" height=\"12\" />. We can build an equation of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/4/bf4a868e583c6d4bb3bbf5ebc47af51237255b38.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5\\text{X}-3\\text{Y}=2023$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"128\" height=\"15\" />, where we have to limit the number of moves we do. We can do this by making more of our moves the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> move turn than the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> move turn. The first obvious step is to go some amount of moves in the right direction then subtract off in the left direction to land on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/7/0873e9fed23538e535ac05c3284b86bd7bce6fd6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2023$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />. The least amount of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />’s added to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/7/0873e9fed23538e535ac05c3284b86bd7bce6fd6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2023$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> to make a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/0/1707bb92d96cc71131c614d51b7e7856e684461a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2023 + 4(3) = 2035$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"153\" height=\"20\" />. So now, we have solved the problem as we just go <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/6/b069793d4642cafbc11823085faa4ed78fd08019.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2035}{5} = 407$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"94\" height=\"38\" /> hops right, and just do 4 more hops left. Yielding <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/e/22e5af6c831f4697665b4af8f17609a9b1871d34.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$407 + 4 = \\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}\\ 411}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"158\" height=\"30\" /> as our answer.\n</p><p>~apex304, SohumUttamchandani, wuwang2002, TaeKim, Cxrupptedpat\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Notice that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/1/e41a9d1e440e7624df923e156b232393e9588b1d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2023 \\equiv 3\\pmod{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"144\" height=\"20\" />, and jumping to the left increases the value of Greta's position <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/3/463e9e805999491680f948e17fc2723550b4067a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pmod{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"70\" height=\"18\" /> by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Therefore, the number of jumps to the left must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/7/a97c2add535ba169320b91d28d13841b122c175f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4 \\pmod{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"83\" height=\"20\" />. As the number of jumps to the left increases, so does the number of jumps to the right, we must minimize both, which occurs when we jump <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to the left and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/7/a07bb9ef49849b5f1fa49e0a0fbd16bc045780ed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$407$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> to the right. The answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/8/4088829c6d3235d246a608453009bfe3adb962de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}\\ 411}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"75\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~TRALALA\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/c/84cd22f5bbc076b27187740d3de356410d24e405.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5y - 2023$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"79\" height=\"17\" /> must be divisible by 3. The smallest value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> that will achieve this is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/7/a07bb9ef49849b5f1fa49e0a0fbd16bc045780ed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$407$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" />, which lands it at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/f/21fea9777cdb54e491a901f803dbdd97c18d2a7e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2035$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />. After that, it takes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> jumps back, making a total of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/8/4088829c6d3235d246a608453009bfe3adb962de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}\\ 411}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"75\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~e___\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3.1\">Solution 3.1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3.1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Here is Solution 3 but worded differently:\nWe can to go back <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/e/70e634348f8df9eaeac4ced35db64d08a906532e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3x$\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" /> steps from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/c/44c50540796f3f50358166de93fd66419e585e48.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"18\" height=\"16\" /> steps we took past <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/7/0873e9fed23538e535ac05c3284b86bd7bce6fd6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2023$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />. The other way to say this is we go <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/e/70e634348f8df9eaeac4ced35db64d08a906532e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3x$\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" /> steps from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/7/0873e9fed23538e535ac05c3284b86bd7bce6fd6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2023$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> to get to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/c/44c50540796f3f50358166de93fd66419e585e48.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"18\" height=\"16\" />. What is the least value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/e/70e634348f8df9eaeac4ced35db64d08a906532e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3x$\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" />? We need <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/b/2ab0b39cecc248908bbc2b2218c9497e5ff04b95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2023+3x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"80\" height=\"15\" /> to end in a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. The least value for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/e/70e634348f8df9eaeac4ced35db64d08a906532e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3x$\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" />, which makes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/8/3a8c2556055726b8d197bfc96d5eca303f47dda2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2023+3x=2035$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"141\" height=\"15\" />, is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/7/24754b90f9a3e81104aeed0bb7bd42b382a2b1f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2035}{5}=407$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"94\" height=\"38\" />. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/b/02b4f2b7dee89f5b4eddce63fd4350d460cad88b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$407+4=$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"80\" height=\"15\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/8/4088829c6d3235d246a608453009bfe3adb962de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}\\ 411}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"75\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4_.28Easy_to_understand_and_simple.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(Easy_to_understand_and_simple)\">Solution 4 (Easy to understand and simple)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (Easy to understand and simple)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Greta needs to jump <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/7/0873e9fed23538e535ac05c3284b86bd7bce6fd6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2023$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> steps to the right. Since we want (a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />)- (a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />) that ends in a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. The smallest this can be is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/9/f1965fae079a9ba2c0726c307070c2355dfcb213.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> - <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p><p>We can apply this to the problem; the closest number that ends in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/9/f1965fae079a9ba2c0726c307070c2355dfcb213.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/7/0873e9fed23538e535ac05c3284b86bd7bce6fd6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2023$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/c/b7c41d5d55f66cd4a292a064c28c0c679742c8a6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2015$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"35\" height=\"13\" />. (Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/c/b7c41d5d55f66cd4a292a064c28c0c679742c8a6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2015$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"35\" height=\"13\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/2/972c327fd113f3d2656df81653a53eeaea7f838c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$403$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" /> jumps (every <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> jumps to the right is one lily pad, we will use this later.) \n</p><p>From this, we know that to get to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/1/b910f4dafca80b54c6e7bedf63b6485eebff0764.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2003$\" width=\"35\" height=\"12\" /> steps, Greta would have to jump <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> pads to the left, which would take <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> jumps from the lily pad (every <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> jumps to the left is one lily pad). \n</p><p>Lastly, to get to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/7/0873e9fed23538e535ac05c3284b86bd7bce6fd6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2023$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />, it would take <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> pads to the right, which would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> jumps from the lily pads as well.\n</p><p>In total, this is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/2/972c327fd113f3d2656df81653a53eeaea7f838c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$403$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" /> + <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> + <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/7/2a7175687ac053fd16e00c047312692c905b65fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$411$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /> , or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/8/4088829c6d3235d246a608453009bfe3adb962de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}\\ 411}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"75\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~OddPeppyBoots\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_by_Math-X_.28Smart_and_Simple.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Math-X_(Smart_and_Simple)\">Video Solution by Math-X (Smart and Simple)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Math-X (Smart and Simple)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/Ku_c1YHnLt0?si=E5Vs_ZXCVQzSH7Pl&amp;t=3827\">https://youtu.be/Ku_c1YHnLt0?si=E5Vs_ZXCVQzSH7Pl&amp;t=3827</a> ~Math-X\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_by_STEM_Station.28Quick_and_Easy_to_Understand.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_STEM_Station(Quick_and_Easy_to_Understand)\">Video Solution by STEM Station(Quick and Easy to Understand)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by STEM Station(Quick and Easy to Understand)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/WYR3zWkWCV8\">https://youtu.be/WYR3zWkWCV8</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_by_Pi_Academy_.28Fast_and_Easy.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Pi_Academy_(Fast_and_Easy)\">Video Solution by Pi Academy (Fast and Easy)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Pi Academy (Fast and Easy)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/qJVIN4W2WsQ?si=4xJ8dgkJBbaOOG-M\">https://youtu.be/qJVIN4W2WsQ?si=4xJ8dgkJBbaOOG-M</a>\n</p><p>~ Pi Academy\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.28A_Clever_Explanation_You.E2.80.99ll_Get_Instantly.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_(A_Clever_Explanation_You’ll_Get_Instantly)\">Video Solution (A Clever Explanation You’ll Get Instantly)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution (A Clever Explanation You’ll Get Instantly)\">edit</a><span clas